  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/nh-rsa-data/blob/96bd0a247d4463e2ae692310c0fdd17ec563a46c/rsa_html/XXXIV/374-G/374-G-4.htm",
  "statuteText": "374-G:4 Investments in Distributed Energy Resources. –\n\nI. Notwithstanding any other provision of law to the contrary, as provided in RSA 374-G:5, a New Hampshire electric public utility may invest in or own distributed energy resources, located on or inter-connected to the local electric distribution system.\nII. Distributed electric generation owned by or receiving investments from an electric utility under this section shall be limited to a cumulative maximum in megawatts of 10 percent of the utility's total distribution peak load in megawatts. This limitation shall not apply to energy storage or demand response."
